! species_pot_corehole.cellblock -- APPEND this block to a core-hole .cell (the ones in
! structures/corehole/, which already label the excited atom X:exc). It gives the excited
! species its own core-hole pseudopotential while every other atom keeps the normal OTFG.
!
! The exact OTFG core-hole string is CASTEP-version-specific. DO NOT trust the placeholder
! below -- GENERATE it and read it back at M2. The reliable route:
!   1. Consult the CASTEP core-loss/ELNES documentation + the "on-the-fly" (OTFG) core-hole
!      syntax for your version (`castep.mpi --help` / the shipped ELNES example).
!   2. The core hole is a REDUCED CORE OCCUPANCY on the excited shell:
!        O  K edge  -> 1s hole   (remove 1 e from 1s)
!        Ti L2,3    -> 2p hole   (remove 1 e from 2p)
!        Pb M4,5    -> 3d hole   (remove 1 e from 3d)  [deep; scalar-relativistic]
!   3. After the run, open the CASTEP .castep log "Pseudopotential Report" for X:exc and
!      CONFIRM the excited shell occupancy is reduced by 1 and the normal X is unchanged.
!      That readback is the M2 validation of the core hole itself.

%BLOCK SPECIES_POT
! normal species: blank string = default library OTFG (or name your pot file)
Pb
Ti
O
! excited species: core-hole OTFG. PLACEHOLDER shapes only -- replace at M2.
O:exc   1|1.1|13|15|17|10U:20(qc=8){1s0.5,2s2,2p4}   ! O 1s HALF/FULL hole -- VERIFY
! Ti:exc  3|1.8|...|{...2p5...}                        ! for Ti_L23 runs
! Pb:exc  ...|{...3d9...}                               ! for Pb_M runs
%ENDBLOCK SPECIES_POT
